[Part 1] Euler-Lagrange equations of the action (gamma = 0, static, O(eps))
  K dW_full/du - a0 u/(a0-u) = 0;  R = K dW_rem/du = u**2/(a0 - u)  (R - u^2/(a0-u) = 0)
  Phi-eq == div(grad Phi - K P) - K rho : True;  P-eq == (grad Phi - K P) - R(u) P_hat : True
  balance g - u - R(u) at u = a0 g/(a0+g): 0;  mu = 1 - u/g - x/(1+x): 0
  general 3-D field: |div(grad Phi - K P) - div(mu grad Phi)| = 6.3e-15; P-eq residual 2.2e-15
K1a PASS symbolic 0/0/0/0, 3-D residual 6.3e-15/2.2e-15 exact / <1e-10   PAPER49 action -> div[mu(|grad Phi|/a0) grad Phi] = K rho, mu = x/(1+x): AQUAL
  L_PAPER49 - L_A33(static weak field) = 0;  D7d (P) at L*=0 minus A33 P-eq: 0
K1b PASS 0/0 0/0   A33/DSF-21 form and D7d's (L),(P) at L*=0 give the same AQUAL equations

